<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Powerscreen half-year pretax profit up 20pct.</title>
<headline>Powerscreen half-year pretax profit up 20pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		17.3		   vs 14.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.8		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     20.4		   vs 17.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   152.0		  vs 121.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Tyrone-based Powerscreen International Plc is Northern Ireland's second largest publicly quoted company.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 20.80		  vs 17.31</p>
<p> Interest charge	  0.398		  vs 0.320</p>
<p> Interest received	0.043		  vs 0.096</p>
<p> Tax payable		5.11		   vs 4.29</p>
<p> Net taxed		  15.34		  vs 12.80</p>
<p> Retained profit	  12.85		  vs 10.58</p>
<p> Record date	 December 24, 1996</p>
<p> Pay date	    February 13, 1996</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date  December 16, 1996</p>
<p>	 -- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
